Just had my first healer ascension. After doing the protection
racket in minetown, I got a GDSM from a smoky potion. From then
on everything went really smoothly, I didn't have any major problems.
I didn't genocide nor polypile, but used 4 wishes (GDSM, 2xMM and
a spellbook of magic mapping).

After my kitten named Rreawyn turned into a silver dragon in the mines,
I thought that it would be fun to see how far we could go together.
As a healer, I took good care of him: always checking his condition
with the stethoscope and healing when necessary.

First setback was at Juiblex' swamp, when blowing my whistle to
summon my trusty steed, instead a green slime named Rreawyn appeared
next to me. I had two wands of polymorph that I wasted on the slime,
trying to upgrade my pet into something more dangerous. The last charge
turned Rreawyn into a baby crocodile. I thought that the days of
Rreawyn were numbered. Then, few levels down, I fed my crocodile
a chameleon corpse that turned him into a baby gray dragon. Yay!
The dragon quickly grew into an adult version, and he was wearing
an amulet of reflection that was a big help against all of those
ray-type attacks that abound in Gehennom.

Rreawyn's next ordeal was at the plane of fire, where he
inconsiderately kept attacking the fire elementals until he was
fried to a crisp. I had a wand of undead turning with two charges,
and used one of them on the corpse. Rreawyn had forgot about his
mistress during his short trip to the afterlife though, so I had to
re-tame him with a scroll. I was sure that he'd kill himself again
really soon, but once he started chewing on a minotaur (I think it
was a minotaur, something big anyways), I made a run towards the
portal, drawing all the monsters towards me, leaving Rreawyn to
feast alone. Once at the portal, I used telepathy to see when his
meal was finished, blew the whistle, and off we went to the plane of
water. I was starting to have some hopes that we might actually
make it together!

Something killed Rreawyn right when we arrived at the plane of water.
The last charge from WoUT revived him promptly, though, and this
time he even remembered who he was supposed to serve in the mortal
realm. I left him to chew on some fish while I went to look for
the portal. Found it easily enough, blew the whistle, and jumped
in.. but wait... Rreawyn is still eating. Oh crap. That's what
you get when you play in the middle of the night, tired. =(

So my pet decided he preferred the fishing waters of the plane of
water to the cold beer at the demigod bar, where I'm at now with
this angel dude that tagged along with me during my brief visit
at the astral plane. First altar was the right one. A wimpy
Pestilence was guarding it, but two shots of magic missiles
took care of him. And I was only level 25! It's a very powerful
spell, methinks.

So, any tips on how to ascend with a starting pet? My advice would
be:

* get one that flies
* come up with some means to heal your pet ASAP
* in the beginning, let the pet do the fighting
* in the endgame, keep your pet out of trouble by feeding it something
  big and fighting the monsters at a safe distance
* "oR and some means of magic resistance are essential for a pet
  as well!

